# A loop counter's range under the bindings: the store's `or` of 4·k and
# %tid.x << 8 is an add only while 4·k < 256. With n bound to 32 the
# counter runs 1..32, the address reads, and on an RTX 4090 the store's
# 4,096 L2 sectors (32 per warp request) agree with the prediction; with
# n unbound or 100 the or may set bit 8 and the address is unknown.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/counter_range_bound.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=FREE "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/counter_range_bound.ptx --bind 1:n=100 | FileCheck --check-prefix=FREE "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/counter_range_bound.ptx --ncu %fixtures/micro/counter_range_bound.ncu.json | FileCheck "%s"
FREE: st.global.u32  global store 4 B    unknown: or whose sides may both set bit 8
CHECK: trips = 32
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B  warp: 32 sectors (ideal 4)  [1024 * %tid.x + 16 * k[$L__BB0_2] + param_0]
CHECK: measured L2 sectors of global accesses: 1 lines agree (1 exact, 0 within a range, 0 within a bound), 0 differ
